<h1 class="article-title">Paid Ads Agency: What They Do, What They Cost and How to Hire the Right One (USA 2026)</h1>
<p class="article-dek">A clear guide to hiring a paid ads agency in the US: the services, the fee models, the red flags and the questions that reveal a good one.</p>
<div class="article-byline"><div class="article-avatar" style="background:#4C9C8B;">NK</div><div><div class="article-author">Nathalie</div><div class="article-role">Consultant, Tycoon Clap</div></div><div class="article-time">12 min read</div></div>
<div class="article-hero-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 240 160" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="28" y="20" width="184" height="120" rx="14" fill="#FDEED0"/><rect x="44" y="34" width="152" height="92" rx="10" fill="#fff"/><rect x="56" y="44" width="110" height="14" rx="7" fill="#E4E8F2"/><rect x="56" y="70" width="128" height="14" rx="5" fill="#357566"/><rect x="56" y="90" width="100" height="10" rx="5" fill="#DCEFE9"/><rect x="56" y="106" width="116" height="10" rx="5" fill="#DCEFE9"/></svg></div>
<div class="article-grid">
<article class="article-content" id="articleContent">
<p>Paid ads can fill your pipeline quickly, and drain your budget just as fast when they are run badly. That is why many US businesses bring in a <strong>paid ads agency</strong>. The hard part is choosing one that earns its fee.</p>
<div class="stat-callout"><div class="stat-callout-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg></div><p>Short answer: expect to pay either 10 to 20 percent of ad spend or a flat monthly fee, usually from $1,500 to $10,000 or more. Hire an agency that reports on leads and revenue, gives you account ownership and names who runs your campaigns.</p></div>
<p>This guide covers what a paid ads agency does, how pricing works, when to hire one and the questions to ask. For channel specifics, see our guides on <a href="how-to-buy-native-ads-traffic-2026.html">native ads traffic</a> and <a href="what-is-programmatic-advertising-small-business-2026.html">programmatic advertising</a>. If organic search is also on your list, compare costs in our <a href="seo-pricing-small-business-usa-2026.html">SEO pricing guide</a>.</p><h2 id="what">What a paid ads agency does</h2><p>A paid ads agency plans, builds, runs and optimizes advertising where you pay for visibility, mainly search ads, social ads, display, video and sometimes native and programmatic. They manage your spend, creative testing, audience targeting and reporting so the budget produces measurable results.</p><h2 id="services">Core services you should expect</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Strategy and channel planning:</strong> which platforms fit your goals, audience and budget.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Campaign setup:</strong> account structure, audiences, keywords, bidding and tracking.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Ad creative:</strong> copy, images and video, plus constant testing of new versions.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Landing page recommendations:</strong> because ads are only as good as where they send people.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Conversion tracking:</strong> call tracking, form tracking and revenue attribution.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Optimization:</strong> bids, budgets, audiences and negative keywords, adjusted every week.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span><strong>Reporting:</strong> clear updates on cost per lead, return on ad spend and what changes next.</span></li></ul><h2 id="channels">Channels a paid ads agency may manage</h2><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Best for</th><th>Intent level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Google Search Ads</td><td>Capturing people actively searching</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Meta (Facebook and Instagram) Ads</td><td>Visual products, local services, retargeting</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td>LinkedIn Ads</td><td>B2B and professional services</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td>YouTube and video</td><td>Awareness and consideration</td><td>Low to medium</td></tr><tr><td>Native and programmatic</td><td>Reach and content discovery</td><td>Low to medium</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="cost">What a paid ads agency costs in the USA</h2><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Fee model</th><th>How it works</th><th>Typical US price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Percentage of ad spend</td><td>Fee is a share of your monthly media budget</td><td>10% to 20% of spend</td></tr><tr><td>Flat monthly retainer</td><td>Fixed fee regardless of spend</td><td>$1,500 to $10,000+ per month</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly or project</td><td>Audits, builds or one-time launches</td><td>$100 to $250 per hour, or $1,000 to $5,000 per project</td></tr><tr><td>Setup fee</td><td>One-time account and tracking build</td><td>$500 to $3,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ad spend itself is paid to the platforms and is separate from the agency fee. A common guideline is that agencies work best when monthly ad budgets are at least $2,000 to $3,000, since smaller budgets leave too little data to optimize. Treat these as typical ranges, not quotes.</p><h2 id="when">When to hire a paid ads agency</h2><ul><li>You lack in-house experience with ad platforms and your campaigns are not profitable.</li><li>You are spending enough that a few percentage points of efficiency pay for the fee.</li><li>You want to test several channels without hiring multiple specialists.</li><li>Your team has no time for daily optimization and creative testing.</li><li>You need an outside view because results have stalled.</li></ul><div class="article-pull">An agency cannot fix a weak offer or a broken landing page. It can only show you faster whether they are the problem.</div><h2 id="compare">Agency vs in-house vs freelancer</h2><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Strengths</th><th>Watch-outs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Agency</td><td>Team skills, tools, multi-channel experience</td><td>Account handoffs and varying team quality</td></tr><tr><td>In-house hire</td><td>Deep product knowledge, always available</td><td>Salary, benefits and one person's skill range</td></tr><tr><td>Freelancer</td><td>Flexible and cost-efficient</td><td>Capacity limits and single point of failure</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="questions">10 questions to ask before you hire</h2><ol><li><strong>Who will manage my account day to day?</strong> Ask for names and experience.</li><li><strong>Do I own the ad accounts and data?</strong> The answer must be yes.</li><li><strong>How do you charge, and what is included?</strong> Check for extra creative and reporting costs.</li><li><strong>How do you measure success?</strong> Look for cost per lead and revenue, not clicks.</li><li><strong>What results have you delivered in my industry?</strong> Ask for specifics.</li><li><strong>How do you handle creative testing?</strong> There should be a weekly or monthly process.</li><li><strong>What will the first 30 to 60 days look like?</strong></li><li><strong>What is the contract length and exit process?</strong> Be wary of long lock-ins.</li><li><strong>How often will we speak and receive reports?</strong></li><li><strong>What do you need from me to succeed?</strong></li></ol><h2 id="flags">Red flags to avoid</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Guaranteed return on ad spend or lead volumes.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Refusing to give you admin access to ad accounts.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Reporting only vanity metrics like impressions and clicks.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Long contracts with no performance review.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Running your ads inside the agency's own account.</span></li><li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#357566" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Pressure to raise ad budgets before results are stable.</span></li></ul><p>For the tracking behind trustworthy reporting, read <a href="the-real-cost-of-not-tracking-your-marketing-funnel.html">the real cost of not tracking your marketing funnel</a>.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<div class="article-faq"><details open><summary>What does a paid ads agency do?</summary><p class="faq-a">A paid ads agency plans, launches and optimizes advertising on platforms such as Google, Meta, LinkedIn and others, handling strategy, creative, tracking, optimization and reporting to turn your ad spend into leads or sales.</p></details><details><summary>How much does a paid ads agency cost in the USA?</summary><p class="faq-a">Agencies typically charge 10 to 20 percent of ad spend or a flat fee of about $1,500 to $10,000 or more per month. Setup fees of $500 to $3,000 are common. Ad spend is paid separately to the platforms.</p></details><details><summary>What ad budget do I need to hire a paid ads agency?</summary><p class="faq-a">Many agencies recommend at least $2,000 to $3,000 per month in ad spend, because smaller budgets produce too little data to optimize effectively.</p></details><details><summary>Should I hire a paid ads agency or do it in-house?</summary><p class="faq-a">Choose an agency if you lack platform experience or time and want multi-channel skills. Choose in-house if you spend heavily, need constant availability and can afford a full-time specialist.</p></details><details><summary>How long before paid ads agency results show?</summary><p class="faq-a">Search campaigns can produce leads in days, but most agencies need 60 to 90 days to test creative and audiences and reach stable cost per lead.</p></details><details><summary>What should I own when working with a paid ads agency?</summary><p class="faq-a">You should own your ad accounts, tracking, analytics, creative assets and customer data. Never let an agency run your campaigns solely under its own accounts.</p></details></div>
<p style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--ink-dim);line-height:1.7;margin-top:2rem;">Fee ranges on this page are typical US market ranges, not quotes from Tycoon Clap or any specific agency, and vary by industry, ad spend and scope.</p>
